# ROMs are never committed (see roms/README.md)
roms/*
!roms/README.md
*.gb
*.gbc
*.sav

# Save states are recorded locally (see scenarios/states/README.md)
scenarios/states/*
!scenarios/states/README.md

# Run artifacts (traces, screenshots)
runs/

# M4 static site: generated from results.json + results_traces.txt by
# `pokebench site build`, not source. Mirrors runs/ gitignored vs results.json
# committed -- rebuild locally, do not commit the output.
web/dist/

# tools/ one-off research probes are kept (see tools/README.md), but the debug
# output they generate on a given machine/run is not: screenshots, scratch
# JSON dumps, and any discovered-route JSON are local, regenerable artifacts,
# not the durable record (that's HANDOFF.md + tests/fake_world.py + the
# scenario YAML). Also matches the `_debug_edges.json` incident (2026-08-06):
# an unauthored, unverified debug dump left on disk, inherited from a
# terminated session, was mistaken for evidence by the next session and later
# found -- on live re-verification -- to contain at least one wrong entry.
# Full account in tools/README.md, which is tracked and public.
tools/_probe_screens/
tools/_*.json
tools/*_probe_result.json

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# Agent tooling and internal working notes — deliberately not part of the public
# artifact. HANDOFF.md is the cold-start state doc (costs, budget, environment
# specifics, unpolished findings); .claude/ holds the repo's subagent definitions
# and skill wrappers; CLAUDE.md is the assistant's orientation doc.
# NOTE: HANDOFF.md was tracked up to 2026-08-04 and CLAUDE.md up to 2026-08-06;
# both REMAIN IN GIT HISTORY — these entries stop future changes being published,
# they do not remove the past ones. Keep writing to both; they are still the
# source of truth locally. A fresh clone now gets neither — README.md is the only
# orientation a new reader has.
.claude/
HANDOFF.md
CLAUDE.md

.vercel
.env*
